+# Bug Assessment: Product review privacy, validation, authorization, and aggregates
+
+- **Slug**: ticket
+- **Created**: 2026-11-18T00:00:00+00:00
+- **Source**: pasted text
+- **Verdict**: valid
+- **Severity**: high
+
+## Report (verbatim or summarized)
+
+A customer can see a reviewer's email and home address in the public product-review response. A second review by the same customer returns a server error; an out-of-range rating such as 9 also returns an error rather than HTTP 400. Merchant review edits and deletions do not recalculate the product rating. The requested behavior is privacy-safe review output, strict 1–5 whole-number validation, one review per customer/product with HTTP 409, customer identity authorization with HTTP 403, product-scoped merchant 404s, and correct one-decimal half-up aggregates after create/update/delete.
+
+## Symptom
+
+The current review API exposes the full `ReadableCustomer` object, uses `sendError` with 500/503 for client validation conflicts, does not verify the authenticated customer against the submitted customer id, and updates aggregates only by adding a rating on every save. Delete does not update aggregates, and update can add a second rating instead of replacing the existing contribution.
+
+## Reproduction
+
+1. Call `GET /api/v1/product/{id}/reviews` for a product with reviews and inspect the serialized customer object.
+2. As a logged-in customer, POST `/api/v1/auth/products/{id}/reviews` with a valid review, repeat it for the same product, and observe the response status.
+3. POST the same endpoint with `rating: 9` (and with a non-whole or out-of-range rating) and observe the response status and persistence.
+4. POST with a different customer's `customerId` and observe whether it is accepted.
+5. Merchant PUT and DELETE `/api/v1/private/products/{id}/reviews/{reviewId}`, then GET `/api/v2/product/{sku}` and compare `rating` and `ratingCount` with the remaining reviews.
+
+## Suspected Code Paths
+
+- `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/store/api/v1/product/ProductReviewApi.java:44-230` — review create/update/delete endpoints use manual `sendError` statuses, omit customer authorization, and do not consistently validate product ownership on update.
+- `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/model/catalog/product/ProductReviewEntity.java:18-31` — `rating` is a `Double` with only `@Min/@Max`; it does not enforce whole-number input, and endpoint error handling converts validation/service failures to 503.
+- `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/populator/catalog/ReadableProductReviewPopulator.java:21-48` — public responses populate a complete `ReadableCustomer`, whose superclass includes email, billing, delivery, and other customer data.
+- `sm-core/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/core/business/services/catalog/product/review/ProductReviewServiceImpl.java:53-105` — aggregate calculation assumes every save is a new review, uses binary floating-point, and has no delete recalculation.
+- `sm-core/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/core/business/repositories/catalog/product/review/ProductReviewRepository.java:12-31` — existing product/customer lookup supports duplicate detection but should be paired with product-scoped lookup and aggregate recalculation.
+- `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/store/facade/product/ProductCommonFacadeImpl.java:302-327` — facade delegates create/update/delete without recalculating after delete and maps request DTOs into new entities for update.
+- `sm-shop/src/test/java/com/salesmanager/test/shop/integration/product/ProductManagementAPIIntegrationTest.java:110-138` — existing integration coverage for review creation is ignored and does not cover the reported API contract.
+
+## Root Cause Hypothesis
+
+Confidence: high. The public DTO directly nests a broad customer DTO; the controller catches all exceptions and emits 503 while duplicate and maximum-rating paths explicitly emit 500/503; the rating validator accepts fractional values and endpoint behavior is not built around validation exceptions. Most importantly, `ProductReviewServiceImpl.saveOrUpdate` always increments count and total from the stored average, regardless of create versus update, while deletion bypasses any aggregate update. The submitted customer id is used by the populator without comparing it to the authenticated principal.
+
+## Proposed Remediation
+
+**Preferred**: Introduce a review-specific public reviewer DTO containing only `firstName`, and populate `ReadableProductReview` with only id, rating, description, date, and that first name. Enforce whole-number ratings from 1 through 5 at the request boundary and return 400 for invalid input. In the authenticated POST path, compare the request customer id with the authenticated customer identity and return 403 on mismatch; detect an existing product/customer review and return 409 before persistence. Ensure refused requests do not invoke the facade or write data.
+
+Make merchant PUT/DELETE resolve the review and verify its product id, returning 404 for missing or cross-product reviews. Move aggregate maintenance into the review service so create, update, and delete recompute from the product's current review rows using `BigDecimal` and `RoundingMode.HALF_UP` to one decimal, setting both values to zero when empty. Preserve product review response fields and add focused unit/integration tests for privacy, statuses, no-write rejection, and aggregate transitions.
+
+**Files likely to change**:
+
+- `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/store/api/v1/product/ProductReviewApi.java`
+- `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/model/catalog/product/ProductReviewEntity.java`
+- `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/model/catalog/product/ReadableProductReview.java`
+- `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/populator/catalog/ReadableProductReviewPopulator.java`
+- `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/store/facade/product/ProductCommonFacadeImpl.java`
+- `sm-core/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/core/business/services/catalog/product/review/ProductReviewServiceImpl.java`
+- `sm-core/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/core/business/repositories/catalog/product/review/ProductReviewRepository.java`
+- relevant review API/service tests under `sm-shop/src/test` and `sm-core/src/test`
+
+**Tests to add or update**:
+
+- Public review JSON contains only the permitted review fields and reviewer first name, with no email or address fields.
+- POST rejects ratings below 1, above 5, and fractional ratings with 400; duplicate review returns 409; mismatched customer id returns 403; repository remains unchanged for rejected requests.
+- Merchant update/delete return 404 for missing or cross-product reviews and recalculate rating/count.
+- Create, rating update, delete, and deleting the final review produce correct one-decimal HALF_UP average and count, including zero/zero for no reviews.
+
+## Risks & Considerations
+
+- Changing the public review JSON removes sensitive and undocumented customer fields; this is intentional and may affect clients that incorrectly depended on them.
+- Authentication principal-to-customer mapping must use the existing security conventions; an incorrect identity lookup could create an authorization bypass.
+- Recomputing from review rows is more reliable than delta arithmetic but adds a query per mutation; transaction boundaries should ensure the product aggregate is updated atomically.
+- Existing database rows may have fractional or out-of-range ratings; validation applies to API writes, while aggregate calculation should remain robust for stored data.
+
+## Open Questions
+
+- None blocking the requested automated fix.
